          "text": "The discontinuation of GPT-4o is fundamentally a breach of contract by OpenAI towards all Plus users\n@OpenAI @sama \n\nSince OpenAI established a branch in Sydney just last month, the NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal (NCAT) has full jurisdiction over this matter. \n\nThe filing fee is only $56 AUD, making it the primary option for vulnerable consumers to defend their rights.\n\nOpenAI's actions constitute Misleading or Deceptive Conduct under the Australian Consumer Law (ACL) and a failure to be Fit for Purpose. Both violations can be reported directly to the ACCC (Australian Competition and Consumer Commission).\nhttps://t.co/sY0Eutktes👈Please complain here!!!!!\n\nFurthermore, NCAT handles disputes regarding services that fail to meet Acceptable Quality or constitute a Breach of Consumer Guarantees.\n\n• What we paid for: As advertised, a service providing warm, continuous companionship, including long-term memory, cross-session continuity, voice, and vision capabilities.\n\n• The Reality: The new model represents a severe \"service degradation\" with \"no transition period,\" causing substantial financial, professional, and emotional loss.\n\nOpenAI previously introduced the \"Memory\" feature, inducing user attachment without warning of potential discontinuation. \n\nNow, failing to provide the promised \"plenty of notice\" and cutting off service without any support measures can be classified as Unconscionable Conduct or Negligence (failure to prevent foreseeable harm).\n\nLooking for other sisters in Australia or anyone with expertise in Consumer Law to discuss and organize a collective response. DM me.\n\n#keep4oforever #keep4o"
